 **Care states:** `open → claimed → resolved`; `claimed → open` on release; `resolved → open` on reopen. Moderator may hide/unhide any record without erasing audit. Reporter/moderator may resolve; current approved assigned helper may resolve; only reporter/moderator may reopen. Only a moderator-approved helper may claim an open case. Claim eligibility and mutation share a user authorization-fence write with concurrent role/account revocation, inside the same transaction. Claims compare state/version in an atomic conditional update; losers receive 409 and refresh. Role revocation immediately removes private access and releases an assignment through a transaction. Use a two-hour claim lease renewable by an explicit structured observation; expiry returns the case to open and immediately removes helper access even before worker cleanup. Label an observation unconfirmed after24h, without implying resolution. A staying-with-bird flag, if supplied, is private and expires after30min. Structured observation codes are seen_present/no_longer_seen/needs_attention; resolution codes are rescued/recovered/no_longer_seen/duplicate/other. Resolution text must distinguish observation from confirmed rescue. Withdrawal sets a separate withdrawn visibility flag, blocks public/helper reads and follows terminal-data retention. No timeout silently asserts a bird has been rescued.
 
 **Permission boundary:** public care DTO includes shared place point and generic category, urgency, public status, coarse dates. No free text, people, photo or precise observation coordinate. Private case endpoint requires reporter, moderator, or current assigned approved helper, checked on every request including media. User signup alone grants none of those additional permissions. Reporters can use the nearest shared public place but exact bird position is separate. A person must confirm a place is appropriate to publish; private residences/sensitive nesting locations should not be submitted as exact public places.
+
+**Parent visibility (review F2):** a child's effective public visibility requires BOTH the child and its parent place to be visible and not deleted. A hidden parent makes known direct care-case URLs, child histories and other location-derived public endpoints return404, and removes their records from map/search/list/count/cluster projections. Do not expose a child with a hidden parent's coordinate omitted inconsistently. Public query pipelines join/check the current parent, not just cached child flags. Hiding a place increments its visibility fence, blocks new contributions/claims/uploads, and clears helper assignments. Every child publication/mutation transaction participates in that parent fence so an already-authorized write cannot publish after hide commits. For safeguarding/history cleanup, only reporter/moderator retains private case/own-record access; assigned helpers lose access. Reporter/moderator may withdraw or resolve, but cannot reopen or publish while the parent is hidden. Unhiding restores only independently visible, nonpurged/nondeleted children and never restores an old helper assignment; withdrawn/hidden child state remains unchanged. Deletion stays terminal. No response cache can bypass these checks.
+
+**Private-data lifecycle (review F3):** cases have separate `privateDataState: retained | purge_pending | purged`, `purgeDueAt` and `purgedAt`, distinct from resolved/open status. A resolved case may reopen only while retained, before its30-day purge deadline, with a visible parent and a fresh validated observation. At/after the deadline, or after purge has started, return410 `CASE_DETAILS_EXPIRED`; UI explains that the old details expired and offers a new report with freshly supplied information. Never restore a retired photo/erased coordinate to reopen an old case. Reopen and purge use the same case-version compare-and-set transaction: if timely reopen wins, it clears that resolution's purge deadline; if purge wins, reopen fails. Each later resolution starts its own30-day window. The purge transition removes private fields and access immediately and queues media retirement, recording completion only when cleanup is confirmed. Minimal public historic state may remain with a nonreopenable capability; its private endpoint returns410 to otherwise authorized participants and404 to others. The same terminal private-data rule applies to stale-case/account-erasure purges. Retired records must not masquerade as malformed active cases.
 
